<%# THE WALLET SIGNAL — which wallet is live, on this page, right now.

    locals:
      variant:  :chip  (default) the navbar pill, on every page
                :panel           the page-level block the cosign ceremonies get
      label:    optional heading for the panel variant

    ONE COMPONENT, TWO SIZES, ONE STATE. Both variants read the same
    Alpine store, so the navbar and a ceremony panel can never disagree about
    which wallet the browser is holding. The store and its eight states live in
    app/javascript/wallet_signal.js; read that file before changing the words
    here, because the words are ITS exports and are asserted under node.

    MOUNTED AND EMPTY RATHER THAN INSERTED. x-show, never template x-if, for the
    two reasons this app has already paid for: a status region inserted
    alongside its own content is not reliably announced to a screen reader, and
    template x-if silently mounts as a no-op when it is given more than one root
    element. Nothing here is worth that trap.

    WHY THE TONE IS A DOT AND NOT COLOURED PROSE. Body text has to clear WCAG AA
    on both themes, and a vivid fill cannot. So the fill goes in a dot, which
    carries no contrast duty, and the label stays on theme ink. The one exception
    is the undeclared-switch state, which uses text-danger-ink over
    bg-surface-alt — a THEME surface, not a red tint, because the ink is derived
    against the theme surfaces and measures 4.25:1 over a red wash. Both rules
    are in docs/UI_PATTERNS.md and both are guarded by a rendering test.

    SINGLE-QUOTE EVERYTHING INSIDE AN ALPINE ATTRIBUTE. One double quote ends the
    HTML attribute, truncates the expression, and kills every binding in the
    component while the server-rendered markup stays byte-identical and every
    assert_select stays green. A JS comment counts.

    IT IS NOT THE SWITCH CARD. app/javascript/solana_stores.js still owns the
    non-dismissible wallet-changed modal and its address-scoped ceremony
    suppression. This is what remains true on the page after that card closes,
    and the whole of what the three cosign surfaces get, since the card is
    deliberately suppressed there. %>
<%
  variant = local_assigns.fetch(:variant, :chip).to_sym
  panel_label = local_assigns.fetch(:label, "Signing wallet")
%>
<% if variant == :panel %>
  <%# data-wallet-signal-ceremony IS THE PAGE SAYING THE BROWSER WALLET SIGNS
      HERE. wallet_signal.js reads it off the DOM, so the fact travels with the
      markup that means it: a fourth ceremony surface gets the behaviour by
      rendering this panel, with nothing to remember and no list to widen. It is
      the same rule docs/AUTH.md already asks of this ceremony — count the
      blocks, not the call sites.

      IT IS WHAT LETS AN EMAIL-AUTHENTICATED ADMIN SEE ANYTHING AT ALL. Such an
      admin reaches all three surfaces and can co-sign; before this flag the
      signal read the same grey 'Managed wallet' whether Phantom sat on a
      declared signer or a stranger.

      x-show honours quiet as the chip does. On a ceremony page the derivation
      can no longer return a quiet state, so this is the second lock rather than
      the first — but if the flag above ever fails to read, the panel degrades to
      hidden instead of to a confident grey dot over two different addresses. %>
  <div x-data x-cloak
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && !$store.walletSignal.quiet"
       role="status" aria-live="polite"
       data-wallet-signal data-wallet-signal-variant="panel" data-wallet-signal-ceremony
       :data-wallet-signal-state="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state"
       class="mb-4 rounded-xl border bg-surface-alt p-4"
       :class="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' ? 'border-red-500/60' : 'border-subtle'">
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted mb-1"><%= panel_label %></p>
        <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold"
           :class="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' ? 'text-danger-ink' : 'text-heading'">
          <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"
                data-wallet-signal-dot
                :class="{
                  'bg-primary': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'success',
                  'bg-violet': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'info',
                  'bg-warning-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'warning',
                  'bg-red-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'danger',
                  'bg-gray-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'muted'
                }"></span>
          <span data-wallet-signal-label x-text="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.label"></span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="text-right min-w-0">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted mb-1">Connected</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-mono text-heading break-all"
           data-wallet-signal-address
           x-text="($store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.short) || '—'"></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# THE OTHER HALF OF EVERY SENTENCE ABOVE — and it has to disclaim itself
        when the session did not sign in with a wallet.

        An admin who signed in by magic link or Google still has this address on
        their account from an earlier session, and rendering it under a bare
        'Session wallet' beside a different connected one reads as an
        authenticated pair that the system has checked. It was not checked: that
        session proved nothing about any wallet, which is exactly why the
        connected one deserves a second look before anyone co-signs. So the label
        and the qualifier both follow walletAuthenticated. %>
    <div class="mt-3 border-t border-subtle pt-3"
         x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.sessionAddress">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted"
              data-wallet-signal-session-label
              x-text="($store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.walletAuthenticated) ? 'Session wallet' : 'Account wallet'"></span>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-secondary break-all"
              data-wallet-signal-session-address
              x-text="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.sessionShort"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-1 text-2xs text-muted"
         data-wallet-signal-session-note
         x-show="$store.walletSignal && !$store.walletSignal.walletAuthenticated">
        This session signed in without a wallet, so it has not proved this
        address. Whatever wallet is connected above is the one that will sign.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%# THE DECLARED SWITCH. A cosign ceremony walks the operator through the
        vault's signers on purpose, and the switch card is suppressed for exactly
        those addresses. Saying so is the point of this panel: before it existed,
        a suppressed switch left the page silent, which reads the same as nothing
        having happened. %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-secondary"
       data-wallet-signal-expected-note
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'expected'">
      This page asked for this wallet. It is one of the signers the ceremony
      declared, so the hand-off card stays out of the way.
    </p>

    <%# THE UNDECLARED SWITCH, IN TWO VOICES, because one of them was a lie.

        For a session that signed in BY WALLET the card is already up: the
        watcher exempts only the exact addresses the flow declared, so this line
        is what the reader still has after they dismiss their way back to work.

        For a session that signed in ANY OTHER WAY there is no card and never
        was — solana_stores.js returns early unless the session is web3 — and
        the old single sentence told that reader this was not the wallet they
        signed in with, which they never did. Same fact, honest sentence, and
        the one population that gets no card is the one that most needs the
        words. %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-danger-ink"
       data-wallet-signal-changed-note
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' && $store.walletSignal.walletAuthenticated">
      This wallet is not one the page asked for, and it is not the wallet this
      session signed in with. Switch back before signing, or sign in again with
      this wallet.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-danger-ink"
       data-wallet-signal-changed-note-unproved
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' && !$store.walletSignal.walletAuthenticated">
      No ceremony on this page asked for this wallet, and this session never
      signed in with one. Nothing will warn you again, so check the address above
      is the signer you mean before you co-sign.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-secondary"
       data-wallet-signal-disconnected-note
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'disconnected'">
      Your wallet is installed but is not connected to this site, so nothing here
      can be signed yet. Unlock it, or connect it, and this updates on its own.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-secondary"
       data-wallet-signal-unknown-note
       x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'unknown'">
      Still reading your wallet. This is not the same as having none.
    </p>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%# THE NAVBAR CHIP. It renders on every page the navbar renders on, which is
      every page but the funnel layout.

      QUIET IS NOT ABSENT. A signed-out visitor with no wallet extension has
      nothing worth painting, so the chip hides — but the component is mounted,
      the store has resolved, and data-wallet-signal-state carries the answer.
      The context exists before anyone signs in, which is the whole reason it
      was asked for; only the pixels are conditional. %>
  <span x-data x-cloak
        x-show="$store.walletSignal && !$store.walletSignal.quiet"
        data-wallet-signal data-wallet-signal-variant="chip"
        :data-wallet-signal-state="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state"
        :title="$store.walletSignal && ($store.walletSignal.label + ($store.walletSignal.address ? ' — ' + $store.walletSignal.address : ''))"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border bg-surface-alt px-2 py-0.5 whitespace-nowrap"
        :class="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' ? 'border-red-500/60' : 'border-subtle'">
    <span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full"
          data-wallet-signal-dot
          :class="{
            'bg-primary': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'success',
            'bg-violet': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'info',
            'bg-warning-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'warning',
            'bg-red-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'danger',
            'bg-gray-500': $store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.tone === 'muted'
          }"></span>
    <%# The address when there is one, the state's own words when there is not.
        A chip that says nothing but a colour is a puzzle. %>
    <span class="text-xs font-mono"
          data-wallet-signal-address
          x-show="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.address"
          :class="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' ? 'text-danger-ink' : 'text-secondary'"
          x-text="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.short"></span>
    <span class="text-xs"
          data-wallet-signal-label
          x-show="$store.walletSignal && !$store.walletSignal.address"
          :class="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.state === 'changed' ? 'text-danger-ink' : 'text-secondary'"
          x-text="$store.walletSignal && $store.walletSignal.label"></span>
  </span>
<% end %>
